body:
The apg opencode integration targets opencode 2.x. Four surfaces agree on one opencode version:

1. the `opencode-suite/` tool plugin — every suite tool runs as an opencode 2.x plugin built on `@opencode/plugin`;
2. the distributed agent templates (`opencode-suite/agents/*.md`) — the frontmatter carries the opencode 2.x ordered `permissions` array, and the `agent-builder` template generates opencode 2.x agents and maintains the repo-root `opencode.json` model map under the 2.x `agents` key (a model reference with a variant joins as `provider/model#variant`);
3. the `apg init` install surface (`rust.apg.install`) — the tool plugins install into the opencode 2.x plugin location `~/.config/opencode/plugins/` under the global opencode config directory with the `@opencode/plugin` dependency, and the apg-owned stale file set prunes apg-owned files outside the plugin set;
4. the user docs (`README.md`, `AGENTS.md`) — the docs state the opencode 2.x dependency and the apg-release-to-opencode pairing: the apg 0.21.x line supports opencode v1, and the apg 0.22.x line supports opencode v2, so each apg release line supports exactly one opencode major.

opencode 2.x reads legacy V1 config, so a repo's pre-existing `.opencode/` files and legacy agent frontmatter keep loading while the product source states the 2.x native shape (`requirements.constraint.opencode-v2-support-window`).

Acceptance criteria: each of the four surfaces carries the opencode 2.x shape; the spine resolves from this requirement through its domain nodes and solution components to the edited code; `apg_spec_lint` passes the structural checks.
